          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em Zero-one measures
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measures"} measures
            whose only values are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero"} zero
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one"} one
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+theory"} probability theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+laws"} zero-one laws
            and more generally to model situations of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodicity"} ergodicity
          %p
            Zero-one measures form a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+space#Reflection"} sobrification of topological spaces
          %p
            The analogous concept for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernels"} Markov kernels
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+kernel"} zero-one kernel
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+measure"} probability measure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is said to be
            = succeed "," do
              %strong zero-one
            %strong irreducible
            or
            %strong extremal
            if and only if any of the following equivalent conditions hold:
          %ul
            %li
              For every event (measurable subset)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mn 0
                      %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                      %mi or
                      %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mn 1
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      p(A) \;=\; 0 \qquad or \qquad p(A) \;=\; 1 .
            %li
              Every real-valued
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/random+variable"} random variable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+space"} probability space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,p)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+surely"} almost surely
              constant (i.e. it is a
              = succeed ")." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  determinstic random variable
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/determinstic+random+variable"} ?
            %li
              Every event (measurable subset)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conditional+independence"} independent
              of itself:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      p(A) \;=\; p(A\cap A) \;=\; p(A)\,p(A) .
            %li
              Every two events
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A,B
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              are
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conditional+independence"} independent
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      p(A\cap B) \;=\; p(A)\,p(B) .
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              cannot be expressed as a nontrivial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+combination"} convex combination
              of other probability measures: if
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi λ
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi q
                        %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi q
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      p \;=\; \lambda\,q_1 + (1-\lambda)\,q_2
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda\in(0,1)
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi q
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi q
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi P
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_1,q_2\in P X
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi q
                          %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi q
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q_1=q_2=q
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+closed+sets"} irreducible closed sets
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              cannot be expressed as a nontrivial
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+mixture"} convex mixture
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p=\mu(\pi)
              for some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi\in P P X
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              is its multiplication), then necessarily
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi=\delta_p
            %li
              For every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g:X\to\mathbb{R}
              for which the integrals below exist, integration with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              preserves multiplication:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi dp
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi X
                        %mi f
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi dp
                        %mo )
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi X
                        %mi g
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi dp
                        %mo )
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\int_X (f\cdot g)\,dp \;=\; \left( \int_X f\,dp \right) \cdot \left( \int_X g\,dp \right) .
            %li The parallel pair of maps
          %svg{:height => "33.467pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 132.159 33.467", :width => "132.159pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
