          %p
            agree on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            denotes the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            is its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+measures"} Dirac measures
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+measure"} Dirac delta
                measure is zero-one:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi A
                                %mo ;
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 0
                              %mtd
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∉
                                %mi A
                                %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\delta_x(A) \;=\; 1_A(x) \;=\; \begin{cases}
                      1 &amp; x\in A ; \\
                      0 &amp; x\notin A .
                      \\end{cases}
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel"} standard Borel
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+measurable+space"} if it has enough points
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a Dirac delta.
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ergodic+measure"} ergodic measure
                is zero-one when restricted to the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+sigma-algebra"} invariant sigma-algebra
          %h2#further_properties Further properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Zero-one measures are exactly the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/law+of+a+random+variable"} laws
                of those
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/random+variables"} random variables
                which satisfy a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero-one+law"} zero-one law
            %li
              %p
                Zero-one measures are exactly the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+category#deterministic_morphisms"} deterministic states
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stoch"} Stoch
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+categories"} Markov categories
          %h2#the_monad_of_zeroone_measures The monad of zero-one measures
          %p
            Zero-one measures form a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S,\eta_S,\mu_S)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+prime+filters"} completely prime filters
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+space#Reflection"}> sobrification
            ) on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            %strong sobrification monad of measurable spaces
            (see also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+measurable+space"} sober measurable space
            %a{:href => "#det_submonad"} MP’22
            (based on previous work, see the references), here we give a more explicit description.
          %p
            In what follows, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-algebra"} sigma-algebra
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_X
          %h3#functor_and_unit Functor and unit
          %p
            The space of zero-one measures
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S X
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            can be equivalently described as follows:
