          %ul
            %li
              It is the subset of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
              (the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-algebra"} sigma-algebra
              induced from the one of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P X
            %li
              It is the set of all zero-one measures on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-algebra"} sigma-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_{S X}
              given by the following sets,
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mo *
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      A^* \;\coloneqq\; \{p\in S X \;:\; p(A) = 1 \}
              %p
                for all measurable
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ⊆
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\subseteq X
          %p The unit of the monad can be characterized equivalently as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              Since every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+measure"} Dirac measure
              is zero-one, the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta:X\to P X
              lands in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S X
            %li
              Notice that by naturality of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              (the unit of the Giry monad), the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta:X\to P X
              factors uniquely through the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equalizer"} equalizer
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S X
