          %p
            (Compare to how a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sober+topological+space#Reflection"} sobrification
            have the same
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
          %h3#multiplication_and_idempotency Multiplication and idempotency
          %p
            We can define the multiplication of the monad, explicitly, as follows. Given a
            %em zero-one measure over zero-one measures
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                    %mi S
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi\in S S X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_S(\pi)\in S X
            to be defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi A
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mu_S(\pi)(A) \;\coloneqq\; \pi(A^*) .
          %p
            Notice that for every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi S
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in S X
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mi in
                    %mi S
                    %mi S
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi in S S X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
